[src('butler_acts','Judith Butler, “Performative Acts and Gender Constitution: An Essay in Phenomenology and Feminist Theory,” Theatre Journal 40:4 (1988), 519–531.','https://web.stanford.edu/~eckert/Courses/l1562018/Readings/Butler1988.pdf','Primary PDF text read for printed pp. 521–522 and 530–531; opening and adjacent fragments inspected while locating pages. No complete-article, visual page collation or book reading claimed. Stanford-hosted JSTOR reproduction; header checks December 1988, DOI 10.2307/3207893. Amherst mirror returned 403. Paraphrase preserves constraints/sanctions and the critique of reifying the category of women.',True),src('butler_berkeley','UC Berkeley Comparative Literature, Judith Butler: institutional author bibliography.','https://complit.berkeley.edu/people/judith-butler','Current institutional profile and bibliography checked for Gender Trouble 1990 and Bodies That Matter 1993; complete books unread. Present institutional co-PI/teaching activity and 2025 award are positive recent life evidence, not a date inferred from absence of death. Unselected coauthored/edited books are not silently treated as solo publications.')],['butler_trouble'],
